# New Classical and New Keynesian Macroeconomics.

**Authors:** Vane, Howard, Snowdon, Brian

## Abstract
Summarizes underlying tenets and policy implications of new classical and new Keynesian macroeconomics. Compares new approaches with orthodox Keynesian and monetarist schools of thought. Identifies the fundamental difference between new classical and new Keynesian models as the assumption regarding the speed of wage and price adjustment following a disturbance. Includes questions for classroom use. (DK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ460309

